1
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:05,630
I can’t read this screen. Help me.

2
00:00:05,730 --> 00:00:08,010
Many people feel this, every day.

3
00:00:08,610 --> 00:00:12,412
AccessPoint. Stuck at a machine? Send a photo.

4
00:00:13,012 --> 00:00:17,007
Machines replaced the counters, just as the world grew older.

5
00:00:17,107 --> 00:00:20,258
And a chatbot that guesses can press the wrong button.

6
00:00:21,012 --> 00:00:24,058
Muse Spark reads the photo and plans one step.

7
00:00:24,158 --> 00:00:27,560
SAM 3.1 outlines every button precisely.

8
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:30,504
Muse Voice hears you in twenty-five languages.

9
00:00:30,604 --> 00:00:33,509
And code points only where both models agree.

10
00:00:35,009 --> 00:00:37,626
It never needs your PIN, and never guesses.

11
00:00:37,726 --> 00:00:41,325
It stops wrong totals. You press every button.

12
00:00:42,525 --> 00:00:46,291
Amara scans the sticker on the kiosk. One button.

13
00:00:46,491 --> 00:00:51,747
AccessPoint: “Put your passport on the glass below the screen, photo page down.”

14
00:00:53,191 --> 00:00:58,733
AccessPoint: “It found Amara Okafor, flying to Singapore. Is that you?”

15
00:00:59,585 --> 00:01:01,791
Amara: “Yes, that’s me.”

16
00:01:01,891 --> 00:01:05,684
AccessPoint: “Would you like a window seat, or an aisle seat?”

17
00:01:11,472 --> 00:01:12,824
Amara: “Window.”

18
00:01:12,924 --> 00:01:18,415
AccessPoint: “Your boarding pass is printing on the right. Gate C twenty two.”

19
00:01:19,115 --> 00:01:23,185
Daniel is blind. AccessPoint guides his hand to the slot.

20
00:01:23,285 --> 00:01:26,620
AccessPoint: “Move down, and a little to the left.”

21
00:01:26,820 --> 00:01:32,622
AccessPoint: “Stop. The slot is right under your fingers. Push the card in.”

22
00:01:33,322 --> 00:01:45,442
AccessPoint: “Stop. This screen wants forty-two dollars for one milk. The milk is four dollars twenty. Don’t pay. Press Cancel, on the left.”

23
00:01:45,642 --> 00:01:52,586
AccessPoint: “Cancelled. Nothing was paid. A staff member is coming to fix the total.”

24
00:01:53,286 --> 00:01:58,156
AccessPoint: “I can’t see the buttons clearly. Tilt the phone up a little.”

25
00:01:58,356 --> 00:02:02,922
AccessPoint: “Now I can see. Window seat, or aisle seat?”

26
00:02:03,522 --> 00:02:06,766
No app needed. The same assistant works in chat.

27
00:02:07,822 --> 00:02:11,969
Muse Spark asks: window or aisle? She taps Window.

28
00:02:19,022 --> 00:02:23,206
On WhatsApp, Siti gets the step in Bahasa, as text and voice.

29
00:02:29,222 --> 00:02:32,757
On Messenger, Mr Lim’s photo gets a clear stop.

30
00:02:37,722 --> 00:02:41,446
Scan the sticker, the chat opens. Nothing to install.

31
00:02:41,822 --> 00:02:45,792
Eight scenarios, six machines, any of twenty-five languages.

32
00:02:46,822 --> 00:02:48,800
We tested it on the real models.

33
00:02:52,022 --> 00:02:55,173
Independence by design. Try it in your browser.
